hey can use it even up to the point it plugs into their brain, they just have to unplug before sunset because the vamp body will try to return to it's natural state unless you have powers supressing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:14:51-08:00","id":778626,"title":"","content":"... Great, I just had flashes of Sword Art Online in the World of Darkness. Guess that mean's Kirito is a nascent Virtual Adept who Awakened in Aincrad. Would explain how he suddenly lucked out and got a &quot;mental health counseling program&quot; AI as a familiar spirit. <br /> <br /> The only other main cast who I could see having Awakened during the game would be Asuna, who I could see being recruited by the Syndicate, given her family's connections. But she's too good a person, and would probably wind up being co-opted by the Celestial Chorus (not because she's particularly religious, but her drive to help people, first and foremost). I could see Agil being the lone Virtual Adept who was already Awakened, which is why he takes a kind of backseat mentorship role to our hero. <br /> <br /> Akihiko Kayaba would be a Void Engineer or Iteration Xer who went off the reservation and took his pet project &quot;public&quot;, in a very unauthorized fashion. After the &quot;SAO incident&quot; he tried his own self-engineered Ascension (Success unknown). Suguha would be a Progenitor or Syndicate officer who tried to sell the tech to Pentex and got slagged for it. I could see the leading trio of Laughing Coffin being Euthanatos who succumbed to Quiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link"