temprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T09:59:15-08:00","id":781736,"title":"","content":"Vampires might be able to use specialized induction-based interface technologies produced by mortal sorcery or the technology-related Thaumaturgy Art to hook into virtual reality. Alternatively, they can potentially use Auspex's ability to astrally project to directly send their mind into the virtual realm created by the game. I'd expect that the VR equipment could act as a sort-of arcane/sympathetic link that would .<br /> <br /> That place is fairly Weaver-tied, but there's no <i>particular</i> reason not to get such a thing for say Glass Walkers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/771717-virtual-reality-mmos-and-other-technology?p=778626#post778626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Great, I just had flashes of Sword Art Online in the World of Darkness. Guess that mean's Kirito is a nascent Virtual Adept who Awakened in Aincrad. Would explain how he suddenly lucked out and got a &quot;mental health counseling program&quot; AI as a familiar spirit.<br /> <br /> The only other main cast who I could see having Awakened during the game would be Asuna, who I could see being recruited by the Syndicate, given her family's connections. But she's too good a person, and would probably wind up being co-opted by the Celestial Chorus (not because she's particularly religious, but her drive to help people, first and foremost). I could see Agil being the lone Virtual Adept who was already Awakened, which is why he takes a kind of backseat mentorship role to our hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can have a drive to help people without being a Chorister; the Chorister approach is &quot;all faiths are one&quot;, not &quot;altruism&quot;. They do a lot of altruism as a result but there's no particular reason that someone has to be of their particular philosophical club to help out. Even a Syndic who's into the &quot;invest in people&quot; side of things might be able to get in on that, even if they'd be watched more closely for &quot;potential Deviant sympathies&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Akihiko Kayaba would be a Void Engineer or Iteration Xer who went off the reservation and took his pet project &quot;public&quot;, in a very unauthorized fashion. After the &quot;SAO incident&quot; he tried his own self-engineered Ascension (Success unknown). Suguha would be a Progenitor or Syndicate officer who tried to sell the tech to Pentex and got slagged for it. I could see the leading trio of Laughing Coffin being Euthanatos who succumbed to Quiet. </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough? His approach sounds a <i>lot</i> more like a <i>really unhinged</i> survival-of-the-elitest Virtual Adept, given he's effectively trying to force what is effectively a perversion of the Adept view of Ascension onto his players. Sword Art Online could well just be an attempt to show the viability of his views and force Awakenings in those who survive.<br /> <br /> All the factions have their dark sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:16:27-08:00","id":781761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/771717-virtual-reality-mmos-and-other-technology?p=781736#post781736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funnily enough? His approach sounds a <i>lot</i> more like a <i>really unhinged</i> survival-of-the-elitest Virtual Adept, given he's effectively trying to force what is effectively a perversion of the Adept view of Ascension onto his players. Sword Art Online could well just be an attempt to show the viability of his views and force Awakenings in those who survive.<br /> <br /> All the factions have their dark sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a popular misconception that he was TRYING to get people killed, in an almost Hunger-Games-ish scenario. Really, survival of the fittest had absolutely nothing to do with it. Kayaba's ambition was to create a world, a true reality in the virtual plane. And for it to be *real*, there had to be consequences. There had to be DEATH. I took him to be a high functioning sociopath who didn't set out to get people killed in and of itself, but was too detached from the human condition to really understand that what he was doing was HORRIBLE. He had a dream, and he was going to achieve it.<br /> <br /> Whether or not people died, that would be because of their own choices and actions. He simply enabled the option for death to be a very real consequence of those actions. Y'know, just like real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:57:37-08:00","id":781775,"title":"","content":"Hm, fair. That still sounds very strongly like a VA approach to things; their whole &quot;upload everybody to the internet&quot; Ascension plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:34:57-08:00","id":807308,"title":"","content":"curious thoughts on how Drones, and such are used in modern Elyisum freeholds or septs.... expect any caern not of the talons to have a few discreet drones buzzing around...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.images