o-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/771717-virtual-reality-mmos-and-other-technology?p=807447#post807447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok... a sept can have spirits... but a freehold, or elysium?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both existed long before drones came along.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:07:02-08:00","id":808352,"title":"","content":"I once suggested a game rather like SAO with MtAs and his historical counterparts but it never got past that stage and it was probably a little bit too ambitious.<br /> <br /> The backstory was that the 'Kayaba' behind this was an older mage that had started as Virtual Adept but defected to the Technocracy. However he had two constants in his time with both groups, his charisma and his obsession with the Digital Web, virtual reality and Ascension. He didn't create the virtual world of his alone and has with him a group of like-minded Technocrats and Traditionalists. But as far as they were concerned it was to be a safe testbed for experiments on Awakening sleepers and the like. Kayaba on the other hand, had privately come to the conclusion that an Awakening could not happen in a safe, risk-free environment and that only by struggling and risking life could one truly Awakening. As a result, on the day the game went live, he either murderer or trapped nearly all his comrades within the game.<br /> <br /> The virtual world would be the world of Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade, albeit in a fictional world with the Order of Reason and the Nine Traditions set against each other. Indeed Kayaba would announce to the players that only way to win was for one group to win the Ascension War, freeing them and only them.<br /> <br /> The group would either be a group of players trying to survive and escape the game, or a group of mages and/or technocrats trying to uncover Kayaba's whereabouts and try to free the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T19:26:58-08:00","id":808384,"title":"","content":"oh am playing arkham knight... think its good inspiration with its drones for what the Technocracy, pentex, or a DESPERATE glasswalker might create","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" cl